---
import CompareLayout from '../../layouts/CompareLayout.astro';
import { withBase } from '../../lib/urls';

const appStoreUrl = 'https://apps.shopify.com/blocklist';
---

<CompareLayout
	title="Blox vs Blockify: Block Customers or Block Visitors?"
	description="Blox blocks customers by email, phone, address or payment, shared across stores. Blockify blocks visitors by IP, country, VPN and bots. See which fits."
>
	<span class="section-label">Comparison</span>
	<h1>Blox vs Blockify: block customers or block visitors?</h1>
	<p class="section-lead">
		Blox and Blockify both block things on Shopify, but different things. <strong>Blox blocks customers</strong>: people you, or another store, have already decided not to ship to. <strong>Blockify blocks visitors</strong>: traffic by IP, country, VPN, and bots. Here’s a fair head-to-head. For NoFraud and Signifyd as well, see <a href={withBase('compare/')}>Blox vs NoFraud, Signifyd, and Blockify</a>. Monthly network stats: <a href={withBase('fraud-index/')}>Blox Fraud Index</a>.
	</p>

	<section class="compare__block" aria-labelledby="positioning">
		<h2 id="positioning">The short version</h2>
		<p>
			<strong>Blox</strong> is a customer blocklist. Block fraudsters, chargeback abusers,
			serial returners, and refund abusers by email, phone, address, or payment method, and
			their next order is held or cancelled before fulfillment. Past chargebacks are imported
			when you install, and the community blocklist, included on every plan, flags customers
			blocked by other Blox stores.
		</p>
		<p>
			<strong>Blockify</strong> blocks visitors by IP address, country, VPN, proxy, and bots.
			It works on traffic, not on a customer you have already decided not to ship to.
		</p>
		<p>
			If your problem is <strong>repeat chargebacks</strong>, refund abuse, or the same
			customer coming back under a new email, Blox is built for it.
		</p>
	</section>

	<section class="compare__block" aria-labelledby="table-heading">
		<h2 id="table-heading">Side-by-side</h2>
		<div class="compare__table-wrap">
			<table>
				<thead>
					<tr>
						<th>Dimension</th>
						<th>Blox</th>
						<th>Blockify</th>
					</tr>
				</thead>
				<tbody>
					<tr>
						<th scope="row">Primary model</th>
						<td>Blocks customers by email, phone, address, or payment</td>
						<td>Blocks visitors by IP, country, VPN, proxy, and bots</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<th scope="row">Best against</th>
						<td>Chargebacks, serial returners, refund abuse, duplicate accounts</td>
						<td>Bots, unwanted countries, VPN and proxy traffic</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<th scope="row">Where it acts</th>
						<td>Holds or cancels the customer’s order before fulfillment</td>
						<td>Blocks the visit</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<th scope="row">Cross-store memory</th>
						<td>Yes: community blocklist on every plan, including Free</td>
						<td>Not a shared customer blocklist</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<th scope="row">Pricing</th>
						<td>
							Free under 100 orders/month; $19, $49, or $99/month. No per-transaction fees.
							<a href={appStoreUrl} rel="noopener noreferrer">Blox on the App Store</a>
						</td>
						<td>Subscription plans for filter rules</td>
					</tr>
				</tbody>
			</table>
		</div>
	</section>

	<p class="compare__cta">
		<a class="btn" href={appStoreUrl} rel="noopener noreferrer">Install Blox on Shopify</a>
	</p>
	<p class="compare__more">
		<a href={withBase('compare/')}>Blox vs NoFraud, Signifyd, and Blockify</a>
		<span aria-hidden="true">·</span>
		<a href={withBase('fraud-index/')}>Blox Fraud Index</a>
		<span aria-hidden="true">·</span>
		<a href={withBase('faq/')}>FAQ</a>
		<span aria-hidden="true">·</span>
		<a href={withBase('guides/chargeback-blacklist/')}>What is a chargeback blacklist?</a>
		<span aria-hidden="true">·</span>
		<a href={withBase('guides/how-to-block-repeat-chargeback-customers/')}>How to block repeat chargeback customers</a>
		<span aria-hidden="true">·</span>
		<a href={withBase('guides/blocklist-vs-fraud-filter/')}>Blocklist vs fraud filter</a>
		<span aria-hidden="true">·</span>
		<a href={withBase('guides/how-to-block-a-customer-on-shopify/')}>How to block a customer on Shopify</a>
	</p>
</CompareLayout>
